1. Sort an Array (Ascending)
import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 2, 8, 1, 9};

        Arrays.sort(arr);

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));
    }
}


Sort an Array (Descending)

For primitive arrays, sort in ascending order and then reverse:

import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 2, 8, 1, 9};

        Arrays.sort(arr);

        for (int i = arr.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
        }
    }
}
